  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><mi>q</mi></math> are two statements, then which of the following statement is a tautology"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∨</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>p</mi><mo>⇔</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></math></p><p>We know,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;is always true</p><p>i.e. the given statement is always true, hence, a tautology</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
